# AI Emergency Traffic Corridor — Project Evidence

## 1. Project Overview
This project explores the use of Artificial Intelligence (AI) to reduce delays faced by emergency vehicles due to traffic congestion and red signals.

## 2. Problem Statement
Emergency vehicles lose critical response time because congestion along their routes is not identified early and traffic signals are not cleared in time.

## 3. Project Objective
- Identify congestion along emergency routes.
- Analyse available traffic data.
- Explore congestion-aware route suggestions.
- Support traffic signal coordination with authorized human supervision.
- Improve emergency response efficiency while maintaining safety.

## 4. Customer and Stakeholders
- Ambulance and fire-engine drivers
- Emergency dispatchers
- Traffic controllers and traffic police
- City traffic authorities
- Patients and the public

## 5. Evidence to Be Collected
- Emergency driver interviews
- Dispatcher and traffic controller feedback
- Permitted traffic observations
- Authorized traffic and signal data
- Testing and evaluation results

## 6. Proposed Approach
Analyse permitted traffic data to identify congestion and possible delays along emergency routes. Explore route suggestions and signal coordination under authorized human supervision.

## 7. Safety and Privacy
No live traffic signals or emergency vehicles will be tested without authorization and appropriate safety controls. Personal data, credentials and confidential information must not be published.

## 8. Current Status
Problem validation and planning stage. Actual time savings, AI accuracy and system reliability are yet to be measured.
